WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.224
Suppose the search range is already
chosen.

2
00:00:03.224 --> 00:00:06.098
Each dot is a candidate parameter vector.

3
00:00:06.098 --> 00:00:10.204
Sobol organizes where we evaluate the
model inside that range.

4
00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:13.805
This low-discrepancy design spreads

5
00:00:13.805 --> 00:00:16.716
candidates through the box in a structured
way.

6
00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:20.354
Here are the first sixty-four points from
the saved search.

7
00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:29.199
The full design has five hundred twelve
points, a power of two.

8
00:00:29.199 --> 00:00:34.049
Horizontal position is sigma, vertical
position is N, and color represents zeta.

9
00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:38.120
Sobol supplies candidate parameters.

10
00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:42.547
A separate random generator supplies
shocks inside each simulated economy.

11
00:00:42.547 --> 00:00:44.760
Choosing search locations and choosing

12
00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:47.416
economic shocks are two different
operations.
